implementationPlan.description:
TESTS FIRST (red). Load test-driven-development.

Edit the LANDED bytes. task-43088e9b (verified-local under deliveryPolicy legacy) and CQ-V06 (task-6a5d5a13) both edit policy.ts, and 43088e9b also edits requiredChecks.strong.test.ts. Both land before this row through dependsOn. Re-read policy.ts (evaluateDeliveryEvidence, protectedCheckShortfall, TOKEN_REASONS, describeMissingEvidence), requiredChecks.ts and the verified-local fixture in requiredChecks.strong.test.ts first.

In packages/moe-daemon/src/delivery/requiredChecks.strong.test.ts, reuse its verified-local fixture: an approved snapshot, a candidate whose protectedEntries equal it, and a runner-observed exit-0 run of each approved command on the candidate's tree in an approved environment.

ROWS (prefix UC):
- UC1, the classifier untrustedArchitectureChecks(defs), table-driven. Each case expects exactly the listed ids.
  - Accepted (no id):
    - 'moe-daemon check-architecture --rules arch.json';
    - the same with --base <40-hex> --tree HEAD;
    - the same with surrounding whitespace, which is trimmed;
    - 'npm test', which neither mentions the checker nor protects its sources.
  - Refused (its id). The command mentions check-architecture (case-insensitive), or its scripts include a path ending 'src/commands/checkArchitecture.ts' or 'src/delivery/architectureRules.ts', and it is not exactly the installed form:
    - 'node packages/moe-daemon/dist/index.js check-architecture --rules arch.json';
    - 'npx moe-daemon check-architecture ...';
    - './node_modules/.bin/moe-daemon check-architecture';
    - 'MOE_X=1 moe-daemon check-architecture';
    - the installed form followed by '; true', '&& node x.js', '| cat', '$(id)', a backtick, or a newline;
    - a quoted argument;
    - two spaces between words;
    - 'npm run arch' whose scripts list packages/moe-daemon/src/commands/checkArchitecture.ts.
- UC2, delivery under verified-local (DoD 1). An approved def running 'node packages/moe-daemon/dist/index.js check-architecture --rules arch.json' has every other piece of evidence satisfied, including a passing runner run and equal protectedEntries. evaluateDeliveryEvidence answers satisfied false, and missingEvidence is exactly ['required-check-untrusted-checker:<id>']. This is the case of a candidate-built checker that passes because the candidate edited a module it imports: it can never deliver.
- UC3: the same fixture with the installed form answers satisfied true.
- UC4, legacy and observe unchanged (DoD 2): the UC2 definitions under the legacy profile, and under observe with a strict deliveryPolicy, give byte-identical results with and without the new rule. No new token appears.
- UC5: describeMissingEvidence('required-check-untrusted-checker:<id>') names the id and the installed form, and quotes nothing from candidate data.

RED proof: run the step-4 command. The UC rows fail for the expected reason; every other row passes. Record it.

Size budget: 120 test lines or fewer, table-driven.

Error handling in the tests: assertions name fixed tokens, never messages, and no row spawns a process or reaches the network.
